# patches/linux_mainline/series — quilt-style ordered apply list.
# One filename per line (relative to this dir). '#' = comment, blank lines OK.
# Applied by scripts/apply-series.sh via `git am` (run from the linux tree).
#
# RK3506 pinctrl+clk are already mainline; this series is the board/DT/driver
# delta on top of SoC support. Regenerated 2026-06-16 from explore/linux
# (base v7.1 = 8cd9520d3) via `git format-patch`; reproduces the board-verified
# boot (RW UBIFS rootfs, cold-reboot persistent, 3-cycle stress passed).

0001-ARM-dts-rockchip-add-rk3506-SoC-AES-RK3506B-board-DT.patch
0002-ARM-dts-rockchip-rk3506b-aes-enable-SFC-W25N04KV-SPI.patch
# SFC sampling delay-line tuning — fixes high-speed read ECC errors by writing
# SFC_DLL_CTRL0 (vendor rockchip_sfc_delay_lines_tuning ported). Widest-window
# scan + dev_info diagnostics; THRESHOLD 24MHz so 50MHz still trains.
0003-spi-rockchip-sfc-add-sampling-delay-line-tuning-for-.patch
# Persistent-rootfs bootargs (ubi.mtd=5 root=ubi0:rootfs rootfstype=ubifs rw).
0004-ARM-dts-rockchip-rk3506b-aes-add-persistent-rootfs-b.patch
# SFC 80MHz + rockchip,max-dll (intermediate state; 0006 lowers to 50MHz where
# the DLL window is 230 cells vs ~70 at 80MHz on this board).
0005-ARM-dts-rockchip-rk3506b-aes-raise-SFC-to-80-MHz-add.patch
# RW rootfs root-cause fix (board-verified 2026-06-16): port the vendor fspi
# write-reliability mechanisms the mainline driver lacked — SFC_CTRL_WPEN
# (BIT29, WP#/IO2 driving) per op + a per-transfer power-good gate polling
# GRF_PMU+0x100 bit0 (compatible rockchip,rk3506-fspi, rockchip,grf=<&grf_pmu>).
# Also lowers SFC to 50MHz. With these, Linux SFC writes are reliable (vendor
# parity); the rootfs is Linux-written by forge ubiprog (first-boot) so it
# survives cold reboots. See bringup/nand-rootfs/RW-WRITE-FIX-powergood-wpen.md.
0006-spi-rockchip-sfc-RK3506-power-good-gate-WPEN-DT-50MH.patch
